    ingredients: "2 fresh mud crabs (approx. 800g each, cleaned and quartered, claws cracked)\n3 tbsp peanut oil\n5 shallots & 4 cloves garlic (minced)\n2 inches ginger (minced)\n4 red bird's eye chilies (minced)\n1/2 cup tomato ketchup & 1/4 cup sweet chili sauce\n1 tbsp fermented yellow bean paste (taucheo)\n1.5 cups chicken stock\n2 tbsp cornstarch slurry\n1 large egg (beaten)\nFresh cilantro and deep-fried mantou buns for serving",
    steps: "Step 1: Live Mud Crab Preparation & Cleaning - Humanely dispatch fresh live mud crabs by chilling in an ice slurry for 20 minutes. Lift the triangular abdominal apron and remove. Pull off the top carapace shell and reserve for presentation. Remove and discard spongy gray gills and stomach sac. Rinse body cavity quickly under cold running water and pat completely dry with paper towels. Crack large claws gently with the back of a cleaver to allow sauce penetration, and quarter the main body.\nStep 2: Preparing the Rempah Chili Paste - In a food processor, blend fresh red bird's eye chilies, large red finger chilies, peeled shallots, garlic cloves, fresh ginger, and fermented yellow soybean paste (taucheo) with 2 tablespoons of water until a thick, coarse red chili paste forms.\nStep 3: Aromatics Searing & Oil Separation - Heat 3 tablespoons of peanut oil in a large, heavy wok over medium heat. Add the blended chili paste. Stir-fry constantly for 4 to 5 minutes until water evaporates, the paste darkens to deep crimson, and fragrant red chili oil separates along the edges.\nStep 4: Flash-Searing Crab & Shells - Increase wok heat to high. Add all crab body pieces, cracked claws, and top carapace. Toss and stir-fry vigorously in the sizzling rempah for 3 minutes until shells turn bright orange-red and release a sweet, briny aroma.\nStep 5: Simmering in Savory Sweet-Tangy Sauce - Pour in rich chicken stock, premium tomato paste, sweet chili sauce, rice vinegar, and sugar. Stir to combine. Cover the wok tightly with a domed lid, reduce heat to medium, and simmer for 7 to 8 minutes until crab meat is succulent, opaque, and cooked through.\nStep 6: Thickening the Gravy with Slurry - Remove wok lid and transfer cooked crab pieces to a warm serving platter, leaving gravy in the wok. Bring gravy to a vigorous boil. Whisk cornstarch with equal parts cold water, then drizzle the slurry into the boiling sauce while stirring continuously for 60 seconds until gravy turns glossy, rich, and clings to a spoon.\nStep 7: Swirling Silky Egg Ribbons - Turn off heat completely. Beat eggs lightly in a bowl. Pour beaten eggs in a thin, continuous spiral into the hot gravy. Let sit undisturbed for 15 seconds to set, then gently swirl with a ladle once or twice to form delicate, silky, suspended egg ribbons throughout the glossy chili gravy.\nStep 8: Plating & Deep-Fried Mantou Service - Pour the luxurious, bubbling chili egg gravy generously over the piled crab pieces on the platter. Rest the cleaned carapace on top. Garnish with fresh cilantro sprigs and sliced red chilies. Serve piping hot alongside golden, deep-fried Chinese mantou buns for scooping up every drop of sauce.",
    cooking_instructions: "Step 1: Live Mud Crab Preparation & Cleaning - Humanely dispatch fresh live mud crabs by chilling in an ice slurry for 20 minutes. Lift the triangular abdominal apron and remove. Pull off the top carapace shell and reserve for presentation. Remove and discard spongy gray gills and stomach sac. Rinse body cavity quickly under cold running water and pat completely dry with paper towels. Crack large claws gently with the back of a cleaver to allow sauce penetration, and quarter the main body.\nStep 2: Preparing the Rempah Chili Paste - In a food processor, blend fresh red bird's eye chilies, large red finger chilies, peeled shallots, garlic cloves, fresh ginger, and fermented yellow soybean paste (taucheo) with 2 tablespoons of water until a thick, coarse red chili paste forms.\nStep 3: Aromatics Searing & Oil Separation - Heat 3 tablespoons of peanut oil in a large, heavy wok over medium heat. Add the blended chili paste. Stir-fry constantly for 4 to 5 minutes until water evaporates, the paste darkens to deep crimson, and fragrant red chili oil separates along the edges.\nStep 4: Flash-Searing Crab & Shells - Increase wok heat to high. Add all crab body pieces, cracked claws, and top carapace. Toss and stir-fry vigorously in the sizzling rempah for 3 minutes until shells turn bright orange-red and release a sweet, briny aroma.\nStep 5: Simmering in Savory Sweet-Tangy Sauce - Pour in rich chicken stock, premium tomato paste, sweet chili sauce, rice vinegar, and sugar. Stir to combine. Cover the wok tightly with a domed lid, reduce heat to medium, and simmer for 7 to 8 minutes until crab meat is succulent, opaque, and cooked through.\nStep 6: Thickening the Gravy with Slurry - Remove wok lid and transfer cooked crab pieces to a warm serving platter, leaving gravy in the wok. Bring gravy to a vigorous boil. Whisk cornstarch with equal parts cold water, then drizzle the slurry into the boiling sauce while stirring continuously for 60 seconds until gravy turns glossy, rich, and clings to a spoon.\nStep 7: Swirling Silky Egg Ribbons - Turn off heat completely. Beat eggs lightly in a bowl. Pour beaten eggs in a thin, continuous spiral into the hot gravy. Let sit undisturbed for 15 seconds to set, then gently swirl with a ladle once or twice to form delicate, silky, suspended egg ribbons throughout the glossy chili gravy.\nStep 8: Plating & Deep-Fried Mantou Service - Pour the luxurious, bubbling chili egg gravy generously over the piled crab pieces on the platter. Rest the cleaned carapace on top. Garnish with fresh cilantro sprigs and sliced red chilies. Serve piping hot alongside golden, deep-fried Chinese mantou buns for scooping up every drop of sauce."
