    avg_rating: 4.9,
    rating_count: 48,
    ingredients: "200g European unsalted butter (melted and kept hot)\n250g premium dark chocolate (Valrhona 70%, half melted, half chopped into rough chunks)\n1 cup granulated sugar & 1/2 cup packed dark brown sugar\n3 large eggs + 1 egg yolk (room temperature)\n3/4 cup Dutch-process unsweetened cocoa powder (sifted)\n1/2 cup unbleached all-purpose flour\n1 tsp pure vanilla extract\n1/2 cup raw walnuts (lightly toasted and coarsely chopped)\n1 tsp flaky Maldon sea salt",
    steps: "Step 1: Melting Chocolate & Butter (The Emulsion Base) - In a heatproof glass bowl set over a saucepan of barely simmering water (bain-marie), combine premium 70% Valrhona dark chocolate callets and cubed European butter. Stir occasionally with a silicone spatula until melted, glossy, and smooth. Remove bowl from heat and let cool for 5 minutes until warm to the touch.\nStep 2: Whisking Eggs & Sugars for Shiny Crinkly Crust (The Science) - In a stand mixer fitted with the whisk attachment, beat whole eggs, granulated white sugar, and dark brown sugar on medium-high speed for 5 full minutes. The mixture must become pale, ribbon-thick, and tripled in volume. This prolonged aeration dissolves sugar and forms the paper-thin, shiny, crackly meringue crust on top of baked brownies.\nStep 3: Folding Warm Chocolate into Egg Foam - Reduce mixer speed to low (or use a wide silicone spatula). Pour melted chocolate-butter mixture down the side of the bowl in a steady stream. Gently fold in wide sweeping motions until color is a uniform rich mahogany with zero streaks.\nStep 4: Sifting Dry Ingredients - Place a fine-mesh sieve over the bowl. Sift in Dutch-process dark cocoa powder, all-purpose flour, instant espresso powder (enhances chocolate depth without coffee taste), and fine sea salt.\nStep 5: Delicately Folding Dry Ingredients - Fold dry ingredients into batter using broad, gentle strokes from bottom to top just until flour streaks disappear. Stop immediately; overmixing develops gluten and destroys fudgy, dense texture.\nStep 6: Folding Chocolate Chunks & Pan Prep - Fold in 1 cup of chopped dark chocolate chunks. Line an 8x8-inch metal baking pan with parchment paper, leaving 2-inch overhangs on opposite sides for clean lifting. Pour batter into pan and smooth top with an offset spatula.\nStep 7: Precision Baking Window - Bake at 350°F (175°C) for 24 to 28 minutes. Test with a toothpick inserted in center: it must emerge with moist, sticky crumbs clinging to it, never clean (which indicates overbaked, cakey brownies) and never wet batter.\nStep 8: Flaky Sea Salt Finish, Chilling & Slicing - Immediately scatter flaky Maldon sea salt across the hot crackly surface. Let brownies cool completely in the pan for 1 hour, then chill in the refrigerator for 2 hours; cold brownies set into dense, fudge-like slices. Lift out using parchment overhangs and cut into 16 clean squares with a warm, wiped chef's knife."
