    steps: "Step 1: Draining Fresh Ricotta to Absolute Dryness - Place fresh whole-milk sheep or cow's milk ricotta in a fine-mesh sieve lined with triple-layer cheesecloth. Set over a bowl, place a small plate with a weight on top, and refrigerate for at least 8 hours (or overnight) to drain excess whey. Authentic cannoli filling requires exceptionally dry ricotta to prevent soggy shells.\nStep 2: Sifting Ricotta for Velvety Sheen - Pass the drained, firm ricotta through a fine wire sieve twice using a flexible plastic dough scraper. This traditional Sicilian technique breaks down all graininess, producing an ultra-smooth, luxurious cream.\nStep 3: Sweetening & Flavoring the Cream - In a mixing bowl, fold sifted powdered sugar, pure vanilla extract, a pinch of ground cinnamon, and finely grated orange zest into the sieved ricotta using a silicone spatula. Stir gently just until combined; do not overmix, which thins the cream.\nStep 4: Folding Dark Chocolate & Piping Bag Prep - Gently fold in mini dark chocolate chips. Transfer ricotta cream into a heavy-duty piping bag fitted with a wide round or open star tip (approx. 1/2-inch opening). Seal top with a clip and chill in refrigerator for at least 1 hour to firm up.\nStep 5: Prepping Crisp Shells & Garnish Station - Set out golden, blistered fried cannoli shells on a clean tray. In two shallow ramekins, place finely chopped Sicilian Bronte pistachios and diced candied orange peel.\nStep 6: The On-Demand Piping Technique - Crucial pastry rule: only pipe cannoli shells within 30 minutes of serving to ensure maximum shell crunch! Insert piping tip deep into one end of a cannoli shell, squeeze until filling reaches rim, then repeat from the opposite end until shell is completely filled with no hollow center.\nStep 7: Garnishing the Ends - Dip one open end of the filled cannoli into chopped vibrant green pistachios, and dip the opposite end into diced candied orange peel (or mini chocolate chips).\nStep 8: Powdered Sugar Snowfall & Service - Arrange filled cannoli on an elegant lace doily or white porcelain platter. Dust generously with a snowfall of powdered sugar through a fine sieve and serve immediately with espresso.",
