    author_name: "Chef Yotam Ottolenghi",
    image_url: "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Healthy_quinoa_salad_with_dried_fruit.jpg/960px-Healthy_quinoa_salad_with_dried_fruit.jpg",
    avg_rating: 4.8,
    rating_count: 37,
    ingredients: "1.5 cups cooked white and red quinoa (fluffed and cooled)\n1 can (400g) chickpeas (tossed with 1 tbsp olive oil, cumin, smoked paprika, and roasted crispy at 400°F for 20 mins)\n1 cup Persian cucumbers (diced)\n1 cup cherry tomatoes (halved)\n1/2 cup Kalamata olives (pitted and sliced)\n1 ripe avocado (sliced)\n1/4 cup pickled red onions\nFor Lemon Tahini Dressing: 1/4 cup pure sesame tahini, 3 tbsp warm water, 2 tbsp fresh lemon juice, 1 clove garlic (grated), 1/2 tsp salt",
    steps: "Step 1: Fluffy Quinoa Cooking - Rinse white or tricolor quinoa in a fine-mesh sieve under cold running water for 2 minutes to remove bitter saponin. In a saucepan, combine quinoa with filtered water (1:2 ratio) and a pinch of salt. Bring to a boil, cover, reduce to low, and simmer for 15 minutes. Remove from heat and rest covered for 10 minutes; fluff with a fork and cool.\nStep 2: Spicing Chickpeas for Roasting - Drain and rinse cooked chickpeas; dry thoroughly between paper towels. Toss on a baking sheet with olive oil, smoked paprika, ground cumin, garlic powder, and sea salt.\nStep 3: Oven-Roasting Crispy Chickpeas - Roast chickpeas at 400°F (200°C) for 22 to 25 minutes, shaking pan halfway through, until shatteringly crisp and golden-brown. Cool on pan.\nStep 4: Whisking Creamy Lemon Tahini Dressing - In a glass jar, whisk smooth runny tahini paste, freshly squeezed lemon juice, minced garlic, pure maple syrup, and sea salt. Drizzle in 3 to 4 tablespoons of cold water while whisking until the dressing transforms into a pale, velvety, pourable cream.\nStep 5: Prepping Mediterranean Garden Veggies - Dice English cucumber into crisp cubes, halve sweet grape tomatoes, thinly slice kalamata olives, slice crunchy radishes, and chop fresh flat-leaf parsley and mint.\nStep 6: Building the Quinoa Bed - Divide the cool, fluffy cooked quinoa equally among wide shallow stoneware bowls, spreading it into a generous base.\nStep 7: Arranging Mediterranean Components - Arrange toppings in colorful, neat sections over the quinoa: crisp roasted chickpeas, diced cucumbers, halved tomatoes, sliced kalamata olives, crunchy radishes, and marinated artichoke hearts.\nStep 8: Drizzle & Finishing Service - Drizzle the creamy lemon tahini dressing generously over each bowl. Shower with fresh herbs, toasted pine nuts, and a dusting of sumac. Serve immediately."
