    category: "Vegan",
    origin: "Italy (Ligurian Pesto Reimagined)",
    cooking_time: 20,
    author_name: "Chef Massimo Bottura",
    image_url: "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Penne_med_pesto%2C_cherrytomater%2C_sorte_oliven_og_gedeost.jpg/960px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Penne_med_pesto%2C_cherrytomater%2C_sorte_oliven_og_gedeost.jpg",
    avg_rating: 4.8,
    rating_count: 34,
    ingredients: "350g bronze-die extruded Penne Rigate or Fusilli pasta\n2 ripe Hass avocados (peeled and pitted)\n2 packed cups fresh Genovese basil leaves\n1/3 cup toasted pine nuts (or walnuts)\n3 tbsp nutritional yeast (for rich savory cheese flavor)\n2 cloves garlic\n3 tbsp fresh lemon juice\n1/3 cup cold-pressed extra virgin olive oil\n200g sweet cherry tomatoes (blistered in olive oil)\nCoarse sea salt & freshly cracked black pepper",
    steps: "Step 1: Boiling Pasta to True Al Dente - Bring a large pot of water to a rolling boil and season generously with coarse sea salt. Drop in penne, rigatoni, or fusilli pasta. Cook for 9 to 11 minutes until firm to the bite (true al dente). Scoop out 1/2 cup of starchy pasta cooking water before draining, then drain pasta.\nStep 2: Toasting Pine Nuts - In a dry skillet over medium-low heat, toast raw pine nuts for 3 minutes, tossing constantly, until fragrant and golden-brown; transfer to a plate to cool.\nStep 3: Blistering Cherry Tomatoes - In the same skillet, heat 1 tablespoon of extra virgin olive oil over high heat. Add whole sweet cherry tomatoes. Sear undisturbed for 2 minutes until skins blister and burst, then toss with sea salt and black pepper for 1 minute; remove from heat.\nStep 4: Assembling Food Processor Pesto - In a food processor, combine fresh basil leaves, peeled garlic cloves, toasted pine nuts, nutritional yeast, fresh lemon juice, sea salt, and black pepper. Pulse 5 times until coarsely chopped.\nStep 5: Emulsifying Ripe Avocado - Halve a buttery ripe Hass avocado, scoop out the flesh, and add to the processor. With the motor running, drizzle in extra virgin olive oil in a steady stream for 45 seconds until an ultra-creamy, velvety, vibrant emerald green pesto forms.\nStep 6: Combining Hot Pasta & Creamy Pesto - Transfer drained warm pasta back into the pot off heat. Pour the avocado basil pesto over the pasta. Toss gently with a silicone spatula until every pasta noodle is coated in rich green cream.\nStep 7: Emulsifying with Starchy Pasta Water - Drizzle in 2 to 3 tablespoons of reserved warm pasta water while tossing; the starch binds the avocado pesto to the hot pasta for a silky, restaurant-quality emulsion.\nStep 8: Plating with Blistered Tomatoes & Pine Nuts - Dish creamy pesto pasta into warm bowls. Top with the blistered cherry tomatoes, toasted pine nuts, fresh basil leaves, and cracked black pepper. Serve immediately while warm."
