    avg_rating: 4.8,
    rating_count: 28,
    ingredients: "2 large globe eggplants (aubergines)\n2 tbsp mustard oil or vegetable oil\n1 large onion (finely chopped)\n2 green chilies (finely minced)\n1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste\n2 ripe plum tomatoes (finely diced)\n1/2 tsp ground turmeric & 1 tsp coriander powder\n1/2 tsp garam masala\n1/2 cup fresh cilantro leaves (chopped)\nFine sea salt to taste and warm tandoori roti for serving",
    steps: "Step 1: Direct Open-Flame Eggplant Roasting - Pierce large, firm globe eggplants several times with a fork. Place directly over the open blue flame of a gas burner (or over glowing charcoal). Roast over medium-high flame, turning every 3 to 4 minutes with long metal tongs for 12 to 15 minutes, until skins are completely blackened and charred, and eggplants collapse into soft, tender mounds.\nStep 2: Steam Sweating for Effortless Peeling - Transfer charred hot eggplants immediately to a bowl and cover tightly with a plate or kitchen towel for 10 minutes. The trapped steam loosens the burnt skins and finishes cooking the interior flesh.\nStep 3: Peeling & Rustic Fork Mashing - Slough off the blackened skins with your fingers (a few tiny charred flecks enhance the smoky aroma). Discard the stems. Place the tender flesh onto a cutting board and coarsely chop, then mash with a fork into a rustic, smoky pulp.\nStep 4: Smoking Mustard Oil Temper - Heat 2 tablespoons of authentic mustard oil in a heavy kadai or skillet until it lightly smokes, then lower heat. Add cumin seeds and finely chopped red onions. Sauté over medium heat for 6 to 8 minutes until onions turn deep golden-brown.\nStep 5: Sautéing Alliums & Green Chilies - Add minced ginger, garlic paste, and finely chopped green chilies. Sauté for 2 minutes until the raw pungent allium edge dissipates into sweet fragrance.\nStep 6: Simmering Tomato Masala - Add finely chopped ripe red tomatoes, ground coriander, turmeric, Kashmiri chili powder, and sea salt. Cook down over medium heat for 5 minutes, pressing tomatoes with a spatula until oil begins to separate from the masala.\nStep 7: Integrating Smoky Roasted Eggplant - Fold the mashed smoky eggplant pulp into the bubbling tomato masala. Cook over low heat for 6 to 8 minutes, stirring frequently so the smoky charred eggplant absorbs the spices and aromatics.\nStep 8: Garnish & Tandoori Roti Service - Finish with a pinch of garam masala and a squeeze of fresh lime juice. Stir well, transfer to a serving bowl, and shower with fresh chopped cilantro leaves. Serve piping hot with whole wheat tandoori rotis or parathas.",
