    avg_rating: 4.8,
    rating_count: 40,
    ingredients: "1 large head fresh cauliflower (cut into bite-sized 'wing' florets)\nFor Crispy Batter: 3/4 cup all-purpose flour, 1 tsp garlic powder, 1 tsp onion powder, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp salt, 3/4 cup water or unsweetened plant milk\n1.5 cups panko breadcrumbs\nFor Buffalo Glaze: 1/2 cup Frank's RedHot original cayenne pepper sauce, 3 tbsp melted coconut oil or vegan butter, 1 tbsp pure maple syrup\nCelery sticks & vegan ranch dip for serving",
    steps: "Step 1: Cutting Cauliflower into Uniform Florets - Wash a fresh head of cauliflower and pat dry. Cut into bite-sized florets (approx. 1.5 to 2 inches) with short stems. Uniform sizing guarantees even cooking and crispness.\nStep 2: Whisking Spiced Flour Batter - In a large mixing bowl, whisk all-purpose flour, cornstarch, garlic powder, onion powder, smoked paprika, sea salt, and cold water until a smooth batter forms with the consistency of pancake batter.\nStep 3: Dredging & Wire Rack Assembly - Preheat oven to 450°F (230°C). Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper and fit with a metal wire cooling rack; baking on a rack allows hot air to circulate beneath florets, preventing soggy bottoms. Dip florets in batter, shake off excess, roll in panko breadcrumbs, and arrange on the rack.\nStep 4: Initial High-Heat Baking - Bake at 450°F for 20 to 22 minutes until florets are golden-brown, crispy to the touch, and tender inside.\nStep 5: Simmering Tangy Buffalo Sauce - While florets bake, melt vegan butter in a saucepan over medium heat. Whisk in Frank's RedHot hot pepper sauce, pure maple syrup, and a dash of Worcestershire sauce. Simmer for 2 minutes until glossy and combined.\nStep 6: The Gentle Buffalo Glaze Toss - Transfer hot baked cauliflower florets into a large metal bowl. Pour warm buffalo sauce over them and toss gently with a silicone spatula until every crevice is glazed in vibrant red sauce.\nStep 7: The Second Crisp Bake - Return sauced florets to the wire rack on the baking sheet. Bake for an additional 7 to 9 minutes until the buffalo glaze bakes on, bubbles, and caramelizes into a crispy outer crust.\nStep 8: Plating with Creamy Garlic Herb Dip - Transfer piping hot buffalo cauliflower wings to a serving platter. Serve alongside crisp celery sticks, carrot batons, and a bowl of chilled vegan garlic herb ranch dip."
