    rating_count: 43,
    ingredients: "2 ripe Hass avocados (soft to gentle pressure, peeled and pitted)\n100g premium dark chocolate (70% cacao, melted and cooled)\n1/2 cup Dutch-process cocoa powder (sifted)\n1/2 cup pure Grade-A maple syrup\n1/3 cup full-fat coconut milk (or almond milk)\n1.5 tsp pure vanilla extract\n1/4 tsp fine sea salt\nFresh raspberries, dark chocolate shavings, and fresh mint sprigs for garnish",
    steps: "Step 1: Melting Dark Chocolate Callets - In a heatproof bowl set over a pot of barely simmering water (bain-marie), gently melt 70% dark Valrhona or dairy-free chocolate chips with 1 teaspoon of coconut oil, stirring with a spatula until glossy and smooth. Remove from heat and let cool to room temperature.\nStep 2: Selecting Ripe Avocados - Halve two large, buttery Hass avocados that yield gently to soft pressure. Scoop the green flesh into the bowl of a high-speed blender or food processor. Avoid avocados with stringy brown fibers to ensure a clean flavor.\nStep 3: Loading Flavor & Sweetener Components - Add Dutch-process unsweetened dark cocoa powder, pure Grade-A maple syrup, rich coconut cream, pure Madagascar vanilla extract, espresso powder, and a generous pinch of fine sea salt directly into the blender with the avocado.\nStep 4: Pouring Melted Dark Chocolate - Pour the melted, cooled dark chocolate over the avocado mixture. Scraping the bowl clean ensures maximum chocolate concentration.\nStep 5: High-Shear Whipping to Silken Sheen - Blend on high speed for 90 seconds. Stop to scrape down the blender walls with a silicone spatula, then blend for another 60 seconds. The mixture should transform into an ultra-smooth, glossy, decadent chocolate mousse with zero trace of avocado texture or color.\nStep 6: Portioning into Dessert Vessels - Spoon or pipe the velvety chocolate mousse into elegant crystal dessert coupes, martini glasses, or small ceramic ramekins.\nStep 7: Chilled Setting - Cover glasses with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 2 hours. Chilling allows the cocoa butter to firm up into a luxurious, spoonable, truffle-like consistency.\nStep 8: Garnish & Artisanal Service - Top chilled mousse with plump fresh raspberries, chocolate shavings, and a sprig of fresh mint. Dust lightly with cocoa powder and serve chilled."
